  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced effectiveness of labour inspection and occupational safety and health systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Labour Organization (ILO) aims to enhance occupational safety and health (OSH) in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia (KSA) by developing a national OSH strategy. This strategy, to be created in collaboration with KSA&#x2019;s Ministry of Human Resource and Social Development (MHRSD), will outline objectives, priorities, and actions with a system to measure progress. The ILO will also provide technical support for consultative workshops to discuss and finalize the strategy with social partners and concerned institutions. In addition to strategy development, the ILO will assist MHRSD in establishing a national system for recording and notifying occupational injuries and diseases, crucial for prevention and legal reform.</narrative>
  </description>
